Sure! Below is a simple example of an **interactive card** that rotates when you hover over it.  
It uses only **HTML + CSS** (no JavaScript).  

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="pl">
<head>
<meta charset="UTF-8">
<title>Rotating Card Demo</title>
<style>
/* Basic reset */
*, *::before, *::after { box-sizing: border-box; margin: 0; padding: 0; }

/* Center the card on the page */
body {
    display:flex;
    justify-content:center;
    align-items:center;
    height:100vh;
    background:#f0f0f0;
}

/* Card container – perspective gives depth */
.card-wrapper {
    width:300px;
    height:200px;
    perspective:800px;          /* Creates 3D space */
}

/* The actual card – positioned relative so we can transform it */
.card {
    width:100%;
    height:100%;
    position:relative;
    transition:transform .6s ease-in-out;   /* Smooth rotation */
    transform-style:preserve-3d;           /* Keep children in 3D */
    cursor:pointer;
}

/* Hover effect – rotate around Y axis */
.card:hover {
    transform:rotateY(180deg);
}

/* Front & back faces */
.front, .back {
    position:absolute;
    width:100%;
    height:100%;
    backface-visibility:hidden;      /* Hide backside when rotated */
    border-radius:10px;
    overflow:hidden;
    color:white;
    font-family:sans-serif;
    display:flex;
    justify-content:center;
    align-items:center;
    text-align:center;
    padding:20px;
    box-shadow:0 4px 15px rgba(0,0,0,.2);
}

/* Front face styling */
.front {
    background:#3498db;              /* Blue front */
}

/* Back face styling – rotate 180° so it shows after flip */
.back {
    background:#e74c3c;              /* Red back */
    transform:rotateY(180deg);       /* Flip it so it's readable after card rotates */
}
</style>
</head>

<body>
<div class="card-wrapper">
    <div class="card">
        <!-- Front side -->
        <div class="front">
            <h2>Front Side</h2>
            <p>Hover me!</p>
        </div>
        <!-- Back side -->
        <div class="back">
            <h2>Back Side</h2>
            <p>Thanks for hovering.</p>
        </div>
    </div>
</div>
</body>
</html>
```

### How it works

1. **Perspective** (`perspective:800px`) on `.card-wrapper` creates a 3‑D environment for its child elements.  
2. The `.card` element has `transform-style: preserve-3d`, allowing its children to maintain their 3‑D positions.  
3. On hover, the card rotates 180 degrees around the Y‑axis (`transform: rotateY(180deg)`).  
4. Both sides have `backface-visibility: hidden` so the hidden side disappears during the flip.  
5. The back face itself is pre‑rotated 180° (`transform: rotateY(180deg)`), making it appear correctly after the card flips.

Feel free to replace the content or colors with your own design. Enjoy the interactive card!
